    <p>The Khurāsānī geography is the strongest individual convergence. The historical sources name Khurāsān specifically as the daʿwa's recruiting ground (<em>ʿalayka bi-Khurāsān</em>); the hadith reports name Khurāsān specifically as the source of the banners. No other region is involved at the same level of specificity in either layer. The bayʿa principle corresponds to the hadith commands to pledge allegiance — and the pledging-even-under-hardship motif is itself diagnostic, since the daʿwa required physical commitment from recruits who traveled from their home regions to the Khurāsānī base.</p>

    <h2 id="mahdi">Who Is the Mahdī Figure Here?</h2>
    <p>The candidate-identification question is the cluster's organizing political problem, and the answer is not single. The matn families identify the figure at different levels of specificity, and the Abbasid daʿwa was structured to exploit precisely this variability.</p>

